          "stem": "For the function \\( y = (x - 3)^2(2x + 3) \\), complete the following steps.",
          "parts": [
            {
              "id": "y12a-3b-q11a",
              "type": "mc",
              "stem": "a) What is the derivative \\( y' \\) of \\( y = (x - 3)^2(2x + 3) \\) using the product rule?",
              "options": [
                "\\( 6(x - 3)^2 \\)",
                "\\( 2x(x - 3)(2x + 3) \\)",
                "\\( 4x(x - 3) \\)",
                "\\( 6x(x - 3) \\)"
              ],
              "answer": 3,
              "steps": [
                {
                  "explain": "Let \\( y = uv \\) where \\( u = (x-3)^2 \\) and \\( v = (2x+3) \\).",
                  "work": "\\begin{aligned} u' &= 2(x-3) \\\\ v' &= 2 \\end{aligned}"
                },
                {
                  "explain": "Apply the product rule: \\( y' = u v' + v u' \\).",
                  "work": "\\begin{aligned} y' &= (x-3)^2 \\cdot 2 + (2x+3) \\cdot 2(x-3) \\\\ &= 2(x-3) [ (x-3) + (2x+3) ] \\\\ &= 2(x-3)(3x) \\\\ &= 6x(x-3) \\end{aligned}"
                }
